@flexiarg creativity-commons/distributed-monitoring
@title Distributed Monitoring
@keywords monitoring, tests, sensors, self-evaluation, proprioception, Ostrom 4A
@audience institution designers, Producers, reviewers
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade principle
@provenance Ostrom design principle 4A (monitoring users), as transposed in Corneli 2016 (ICCC 2016), Table 2 and section "4A. Monitoring users" (The Painting Fool; Keller 2012). Drafted by claude-16 with Joe, 2026-10-29. Derived from the paper, not mined from runs.
@transposes institutions/monitoring-users
@status draft 2026-10-29; runs correct it
@references [creativity-commons/ARGUMENT creativity-commons/producers-can-modify-the-tests creativity-commons/process-fits-local-conditions]

! conclusion:
  Tests document the interaction of Producers and Place, and the
  monitoring is distributed among the Producers themselves rather than
  held only by one global watcher.

  + context:
    The obvious design is one function that tracks every Producer's
    actions. But what a Producer first produces is sensory data, and
    sensors come with effectors; monitoring is part of any action.

  + IF:
    Many Producers act in one Place and someone must know what each did
    and how well.

  + HOWEVER:
    Self-monitoring can be self-serving; a Producer's account of its own
    work needs a reader who is not the Producer.

  + THEN:
    Each Producer runs its own checks on what it produced (compare the
    output with the input that prompted it, as The Painting Fool compares
    its painting with the snapshot) and writes the result where others
    can read it. A separate party reads that record and judges whether
    the checks were the right ones.

  + BECAUSE:
    Distributed monitoring scales with the number of Producers and gives
    each one feedback on its own actions; the separate reader keeps the
    record honest without repeating all the work.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Example: each FUTON Emacs fix wrote fix-results/N.json from check-fix.sh; claude-16 read every diff and judged test adequacy instead of rerunning.]
